{"id":69,"number":94,"symbol":"Her2","name":"Receptor tyrosine-protein kinase erbB-2 (HER2)","gene":"ERBB2","family":"REC","location":"P","other_locations":[],"cell_rank":1,"mass_kda":137.9,"length_aa":1255,"discovery_year":1984,"milestone":"neu oncogene identified in rat tumours (Weinberg lab)","blurb":"EGFR relative overproduced in about 1 in 5 breast cancers.","drugs":["Trastuzumab","Pertuzumab","Lapatinib","Trastuzumab deruxtecan"],"therapeutic":null,"pathways":["egfr_mapk"],"orthologs":{"ecoli":null,"human":"ERBB2","mouse":"Erbb2"},"variant_count":1,"misfolded":null,"uniprot_id":"P04626","function":"Protein tyrosine kinase that is part of several cell surface receptor complexes, but that apparently needs a coreceptor for ligand binding. Essential component of a neuregulin-receptor complex, although neuregulins do not interact with it alone. GP30 is a potential ligand for this receptor. Regulates outgrowth and stabilization of peripheral microtubules (MTs). Upon ERBB2 activation, the MEMO1-RHOA-DIAPH1 signaling pathway elicits the phosphorylation and thus the inhibition of GSK3B at cell membrane. This prevents the phosphorylation of APC and CLASP2, allowing its association with the cell membrane. In turn, membrane-bound APC allows the localization of MACF1 to the cell membrane, which is required for microtubule capture and stabilization","sequence":"","pdb_ids":["1MFG","8VB5","8JYR","8U8X","8JYQ","7PCD","1MFL","5TQS","4GFU","6LBX","9IUT","3PP0"],"alphafold_url":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P04626-F1-model_v6.pdb","variants":[{"change":"Gene amplification","disease":"HER2-positive breast and gastric cancer","note":null}],"partners":[{"id":68,"symbol":"Egfr","name":"Epidermal growth factor receptor","score":0.999,"effect_out":"regulates","effect_in":"activates"},{"id":46,"symbol":"Hsp9","name":"Heat shock protein HSP 90-alpha","score":0.999,"effect_out":null,"effect_in":"regulates"},{"id":160,"symbol":"Egf","name":"Pro-epidermal growth factor","score":0.9